---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro'

const OFFICIAL = [
  { id: 'r60', name: 'OIML R 60:2021 — Load cells', note: 'The reference SMART model — the only official pilot. Classification, MPE envelopes, the conformance tests, the R 60-3 forms.', reader: '/studio/view' },
]

const DEMOS = [
  { id: 'r91', name: 'OIML R 91:2025 — Traffic speed meters', note: 'Demo model. Speed measurement: the operational envelope and its disturbance tests.' },
  { id: 'r129', name: 'OIML R 129:2020 — Multi-dimensional measuring instruments', note: 'Demo model. Dimensional metrology with multi-axis measurands.' },
  { id: 'r144', name: 'OIML R 144:2013 — Gas analytical systems', note: 'Demo model. CO and NOx in stationary source emissions: per-channel measurands and the sampling-line subsystem.' },
]
---

<Base title="The live models" description="R 60 is the official SMART pilot; R 91, R 129, and R 144 are demo models.">
  <main class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 py-14 docs-body">
    <p class="font-mono text-xs tracking-widest uppercase text-ink-muted mb-3">SMART Recommendations · Demo</p>
    <h1 class="font-serif text-3xl font-semibold text-ink mb-6">The live models</h1>
    <p>R 60 is the reference SMART model — the only official pilot. The other three are demo models, built to exercise the method on other instrument families. Each renders from its model: the terminology, the requirements, the conformance tests, the report forms, and the certification workflow that runs on them.</p>

    <h2 class="font-serif text-lg font-semibold text-ink mt-8 mb-3">The official pilot</h2>
    <ul class="space-y-4">
      {OFFICIAL.map(r => (
        <li class="border border-rule rounded-lg p-5 bg-paper-raised">
          <a href={`/recs/${r.id}/`} class="text-accent font-semibold no-underline">{r.name}</a>
          <p class="text-sm text-ink-soft mt-1">{r.note}</p>
          {r.reader && (
            <p class="text-sm mt-2"><a href={r.reader} class="text-accent font-medium">Read the model interactively in the Reference reader →</a></p>
          )}
        </li>
      ))}
    </ul>

    <h2 class="font-serif text-lg font-semibold text-ink mt-8 mb-3">Demo models</h2>
    <ul class="space-y-4">
      {DEMOS.map(r => (
        <li class="border border-rule rounded-lg p-5 bg-paper-raised">
          <a href={`/recs/${r.id}/`} class="text-accent font-semibold no-underline">{r.name}</a>
          <p class="text-sm text-ink-soft mt-1">{r.note}</p>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ul>

    <p class="mt-8 text-sm text-ink-soft">The per-Recommendation pages are served by the OIML SMART platform (the private application builds them from the same models). The authoring documentation for building one yourself lives in <a href="/recs/docs/" class="text-accent">the docs section</a>.</p>
  </main>
</Base>
